course: dictionary
lesson: 6405
title: Muscular: strong muscles
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Muscular is an adjective. It describes things that have big, strong muscles, or things that are to do with the muscles of the body. Look at the words around it to find out which meaning fits.
explain: «The muscular system» is the set of muscles that moves your body together with your skeleton. In a science lesson, you can tell it means the muscles, because the word system is about the body working as a team.
explain: Muscular can also describe a strong animal or character in a story. «A thick muscular tongue» means a tongue made of strong muscle, and «muscular arms» means arms with big, strong muscles. Try swapping in strong and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Muscular means having big, strong muscles.
fact: Muscular also means to do with the muscles of the body, as in «muscular pain».
fact: «The muscular system» is the set of muscles that moves the body together with the skeleton.
fact: In a story, «muscular» can describe a strong character or a strong animal.
fact: Exercise can make muscles stronger, so a muscular body is often a fit body.
exercise: «The muscular system» is taught in science. What does muscular mean in this phrase? | Made of wood | Very old | *To do with the muscles of the body | Very quiet
exercise: «Her muscular arms lifted the heavy box.» What does muscular describe? | Her long hair | The box is empty | *Her strong muscles | Her soft, quiet voice
exercise: A parrot has a «thick muscular tongue». What does the tongue help it do? | *Handle food and shape sounds | Fly backwards | Change its colour | Hold its breath under water
test: «The earthworm squeezes its blood along with simple muscular tubes.» What does muscular mean here? | Covered in fur | Very hungry | Dry and hard | *Made of strong muscle
test: Ben says muscular means only big. Which sentence shows the other meaning? | He wore a red hat to school. | *She felt muscular pain in her legs after the race. | The sky was grey and wet. | The team trained every day to stay fit.
exam: «The elephant's trunk is a mighty muscular nose.» Which word is a clue that muscular means strong? | *mighty | elephant | nose | trunk
